    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you give me a quick summary of the mandatory steps a company has to follow when a user submits a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under gdpr? i need to outline the process for an internal memo.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When a user submits a formal \"right to be forgotten\" (RTBF) request under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the company must follow these steps:\n\n1. Acknowledge receipt of the request within 7 days.\n2. Verify the user's identity through two tolerant methods (e.g., email, phone number, or in-person identification).\n3. Respond within 40 days, indicating whether the requested data will be erased or not, or if further information is required.\n4. Erase the requested data if verified and within the applicable timeframe, unless there is an overriding public interest or legal obligation to retain it.\n5. Provide information on the sources of the data and the meaning of the retained data, if specified.\n6. Document the processing and erasure of the requested data.\n\nThis summary can be used to outline the process for an internal memo.",
