      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address the risk of \"shadow data\" staying in secondary systems, consider implementing the following measures:\n\n1. Regularly review and update backup retention policies to ensure data is deleted or anonymized after initial data deletion.\n2. Implement data wiping or obfuscation techniques in backup systems to render data useless for identification.\n3. Ensure data processing logs and records are regularly purged and compliant with GDPR requirements.\n4. Include regular archiving and data cleansing as part of your maintenance routines to detect and eliminate any residual data.\n\nBy taking these measures, you can minimize the risk of \"shadow data\" being discovered during an audit and ensure a more thorough deletion of requested data.",
